{
  "slug": "ser-estar",
  "number": 3,
  "part": 1,
  "level": "A1",
  "title": "Ser and estar",
  "tagline": "Two verbs for «to be»: what something is, and how or where it is.",
  "goal": "Conjugate ser and estar in the present and choose between them for identity, origin, jobs, location, feelings and states.",
  "minutes": 12,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "formas",
      "title": "The forms",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella / usted", "nosotros", "ellos / ellas / ustedes"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "ser", "meaning": "to be (identity)", "forms": ["{soy}", "{eres}", "{es}", "{somos}", "{son}"] },
            { "verb": "estar", "meaning": "to be (state, place)", "forms": ["{estoy}", "{estás}", "{está}", "{estamos}", "{están}"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "text": "Spain also uses *vosotros*: *sois*, *estáis*. In Latin America, *ustedes* covers every «you all»."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ser",
      "title": "Ser: what something is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use **ser** for characteristics that define someone or something:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Use", "Example"],
          "rows": [
            ["Identity and name", "*{Soy} Emily.*"],
            ["Origin and nationality", "*{Es} de México. {Son} colombianos.*"],
            ["Job", "*{Es} enfermera.*"],
            ["Personality and appearance", "*{Eres} muy simpático. {Es} alta.*"],
            ["Time and dates", "*{Son} las tres. Hoy {es} lunes.*"],
            ["Material and owner", "*{Es} de madera. {Es} de Diego.*"],
            ["Where an event takes place", "*La fiesta {es} en mi casa.*"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "estar",
      "title": "Estar: how and where",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use **estar** for location and for states that can change:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Use", "Example"],
          "rows": [
            ["Location of people and things", "*{Estoy} en la oficina. Madrid {está} en España.*"],
            ["Feelings and moods", "*{Estoy} cansada. ¿{Estás} bien?*"],
            ["Temporary states", "*La sopa {está} fría. La puerta {está} abierta.*"],
            ["Actions in progress (estar + -ando / -iendo)", "*{Está} lloviendo.*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Same adjective, different meaning",
          "text": "*Es aburrido* = he's boring / *Está aburrido* = he's bored. *Es listo* = he's clever / *Está listo* = he's ready. *Es rico* = he's rich / *Está rico* = it's tasty."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
